     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:tahoma,sans-serif\">Hi </div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:tahoma,sans-serif\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:tahoma,sans-serif\">I&#39;m doing CFA using R with 68 dichotomous variables which are classified into six construct per a pre-defined conceptual framework.</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:tahoma,sans-serif\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:tahoma,sans-serif\">I wanted to confirm if I should use WLS of DWLS. Do I need to specify the method in the command, or the software will automatically detect based on variables type and apply appropriate technique.</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:tahoma,sans-serif\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:tahoma,sans-serif\">Thank you</div><div><br></div>-- <br><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_signature\" data-smartmail=\"gmail_signature\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><font face=\"tahoma, sans-serif\">W<span class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:tahoma,sans-serif\">H</span></font></div></div></div></div></div></div></div>\r\n"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
