   "from": "Christopher David Desjardins",
   "author": "189d19347ab44a74",
   "date": "2019-03-13T15:02:34Z",
   "subject": "Re: Query - CFA with binary variables",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\">You need to specify these variables as ordered(). See: <a href=\"http://lavaan.ugent.be/tutorial/cat.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://lavaan.ugent.be/tutorial/cat.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792424149053000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1UA63YHyjaOXdhNfJKB6hz\">http://lavaan.ugent.be/tutorial/cat.html</a></div><div dir=\"ltr\"><br></div><div>By default, I believe lavaan reports DWLS and WLSMV (which it labels as robust).</div><div><br></div><div>Chris<br></div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div>"
    ],
